# Mealie — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/mealie.sops.json.
# No SECRET/SESSION_SECRET (Mealie persists both into /app/data) and no
# POSTGRES_*/DB_ENGINE — this stack is SQLite on purpose, pinned in compose.

# Admin
# The first REAL admin, created by mealie_init, which then deletes the
# changeme@example.com / MyPassword account Mealie pre-creates. The user must
# not be `admin` and the password not `MyPassword` — mealie-init refuses both.
# Rotating later does nothing on its own: change it in the UI, then mirror it
# here. openssl rand -base64 24
MEALIE_ADMIN_USER=idan
MEALIE_ADMIN_EMAIL=idan@idanreed.com
MEALIE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_strong_password

